#
# Format:  <repo-relative path>   <reason>
#
# An entry here means "this file legitimately contains credential-SHAPED
# strings". It is not a way to commit a real secret: every fixture listed below
# is self-evidently fake (FIXTURE / NOTREAL / EXAMPLE substrings) and exists only
# so the redaction and scan tests can assert against realistic shapes.
#
# Both the pre-commit gate and CI print each allowlist hit to stderr, so an
# exception is never silent.

